      "content": "okay fine maybe i got the details wrong but look, even if it's not a \"national collapse,\" there are obviously huge risks involved with any massive immigration shift. can you at least give me a breakdown of the common economic arguments people use when they say these types of policies are bad for the budget? like, what are the actual fiscal downsides that critics always bring up?",
